 the planet doesn’t go back down much, if at all.“Record temperatures immediately become the new normal,” said Stanford University climate scientist Rob Jackson. ___Follow Seth Borenstein on X at @borenbears___The Associated Press’ climate and environmental coverage receives financial support from multiple private foundations. AP is solely responsible for all content. Find AP’s standards for working with philanthropies, a list of supporters and funded coverage areas at AP.org.___Read more of AP’s climate coverage at http://www.apnews.com/climate-and-environment	ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS	https://www.nbcnewyork.com/news/national-international/astronomers-discover-strange-new-celestial-object-in-our-milky-way-galaxy/6281217/	https://media.nbcnewyork.com/2025/05/nasa-eccentric-star.png?fit=1200%2C675&quality=85&strip=all	2025-05-28 15:14:02
